---@field labels? gcp.hypercomputecluster_v1.StringMap Optional. [Labels](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/labeling-resources) applied to the cluster. Labels can be used to organize clusters and to filter them in queries.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time that the cluster was most recently updated.
---@field storageResources? gcp.hypercomputecluster_v1.StorageResourceMap Optional. Storage resources available to the cluster. Keys specify the ID of the storage resource by which it can be referenced elsewhere, and must conform to [RFC-1034](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc1034) (lower-case, alphanumeric, and at most 63 characters).
---@field computeResources? gcp.hypercomputecluster_v1.ComputeResourceMap Optional. Compute resources available to the cluster. Keys specify the ID of the compute resource by which it can be referenced elsewhere, and must conform to [RFC-1034](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc1034) (lower-case, alphanumeric, and at most 63 characters).
---@field networkResources? gcp.hypercomputecluster_v1.NetworkResourceMap Optional. Network resources available to the cluster. Must contain exactly one value. Keys specify the ID of the network resource by which it can be referenced elsewhere, and must conform to [RFC-1034](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc1034) (lower-case, alphanumeric, and at most 63 characters).
---@field reconciling? boolean Output only. Indicates whether changes to the cluster are currently in flight. If this is `true`, then the current state might not match the cluster's intended state.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. Mask specifying which fields in the cluster to update. All paths must be specified explicitly - wildcards are not supported. At least one path must be provided.
---@field requestId? string Optional. A unique identifier for this request. A random UUID is recommended. This request is idempotent if and only if `request_id` is provided.
