---Configuration for Slurm [login nodes](https://slurm.schedmd.com/quickstart_admin.html#login) in the cluster. Login nodes are Compute Engine VM instances that allow users to access the cluster over SSH.
---@class gcp.hypercomputecluster_v1.SlurmLoginNodes
---@field startupScript? string Optional. [Startup script](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/startup-scripts/linux) to be run on each login node instance. Max 256KB. The script must complete within the system-defined default timeout of 5 minutes. For tasks that require more time, consider running them in the background using methods such as `&` or `nohup`.
---@field storageConfigs? gcp.hypercomputecluster_v1.StorageConfigList Optional. How storage resources should be mounted on each login node.
---@field labels? gcp.hypercomputecluster_v1.StringMap Optional. [Labels](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/labeling-resources) that should be applied to each login node instance.
---@field enableOsLogin? boolean Optional. Whether [OS Login](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/oslogin) should be enabled on login node instances.
---@field count? string Required. Number of login node instances to create.
---@field zone? string Required. Name of the zone in which login nodes should run, e.g., `us-central1-a`. Must be in the same region as the cluster, and must match the zone of any other resources specified in the cluster.
---@field machineType? string Required. Name of the Compute Engine [machine type](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/machine-resource) to use for login nodes, e.g. `n2-standard-2`.
---@field enablePublicIps? boolean Optional. Whether login node instances should be assigned [external IP addresses](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/ip-addresses#externaladdresses).
